                            \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $L(5,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $6$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n$M($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $5$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,8)$\n$\\,$\n$N(7,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $8$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nThe architect finds the image of the line $l$ under the action of $T$ and places another highway on the plan from this image. The equation of the line on which the new highway lies, in **standard form**, is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $4$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$x\\,+\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$y\\,=\\,3.$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nThe solution of the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+y+1=0 \\\\ 4x+3y-3=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ngives the point where the highways meet. This solution can be written in matrix form as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the values of $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $a\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,b\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,c\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995865/state.json" "file_sha256" "d237c9fb2e1caaf4727a2be25f6a689a692e883c53df0a9fa599daabfb6ecedc"} {"question" "q-138788" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 3-4\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the solution to this system as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995865/state.json" "file_sha256" "d237c9fb2e1caaf4727a2be25f6a689a692e883c53df0a9fa599daabfb6ecedc"} {"question" "q-138788" "field" nil "attribute" "